"The prognosis is influenced by several factors, including the preoperative PSA of 5.8 and positive surgical margins. The presence of lymph node metastasis was documented pathologically. Countervailing findings include the absence of extraprostatic extension and seminal vesicle invasion, along with no reported lymphovascular invasion. Biopsy-to-prostatectomy differences are noted as the Gleason pattern and ISUP report are missing from the biopsy documentation, while the prostatectomy specimen showed Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2). The nodal status was sampled, which is a positive finding for risk stratification. Prognosis revision would be significantly aided by postoperative PSA measurements and tracking its subsequent trajectory over time. The fixed estimated horizon is 62.79 months. This represents expected follow-up without an event, not a known recurrence date. The sensitivity range is 50.23–75.35 months; its coverage has not been validated."
